4. LICENSEE DATA AND SOURCE DOCUMENTS

The Software processes booking data, ticket records, and payment-confirmation
documents supplied by the Licensee (including GDS text and airline or ferry
operator PDF documents). The Licensee is solely responsible for:

  (a) holding the necessary rights and authority to process those documents and
      any personal data they contain, and for complying with applicable data
      protection law (including the GDPR) in respect of that processing;
  (b) the accuracy and completeness of the data it supplies to the Software; and
  (c) retaining its own records as required by law.

The Software processes these documents locally on the Licensee's machine. The
Licensor does not receive, collect, store, or transmit the Licensee's booking
data or source documents. The Licensor does not control, supply, guarantee, or
endorse third-party data or documents, and is not responsible for their
accuracy, completeness, or continued availability.


5. NO FISCAL, ACCOUNTING, OR FARE VALIDATION — PROFESSIONAL VERIFICATION REQUIRED

The Licensee acknowledges and agrees that:

  (a) the Software is a formatting and transcription aid. It is NOT certified
      invoicing software, NOT an accounting or tax system, and NOT a connection
      to Amadeus or to any other Global Distribution System. It performs no
      booking, ticketing, fare validation, or fiscal certification;
  (b) all amounts, taxes, surcharges, totals, passenger and vehicle details,
      dates, routes, and ticket numbers that the Software produces are derived
      from the documents supplied by the Licensee and MUST be reviewed by a
      qualified person before being used to invoice a client, to submit any
      fiscal or tax declaration, or to enter into any accounting record;
  (c) the Software does not verify that its output satisfies any invoicing,
      fiscal, or regulatory requirement in any jurisdiction, including the
      requirements applicable to certified invoicing software in Portugal; and
  (d) responsibility for every invoice, quotation, amount, and fiscal
      declaration rests entirely with the Licensee.


